IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pip-nouns`
IMPORT `pip-dates`
IMPORT `pip-seat`

-- Worked cases for the seat questions of pip-seat.l4: one or more cases a question, each with the facts a real person in the seat
-- would state. The expected value of every case was worked out by hand from the text of the Regulations (the converter's plain-text
-- rendering, not the official text) before the file was run; a case that depends on a reading chosen in NOTES.md says which fork.
-- A case marked "not covered" asserts the explicit value (NOTHING, or a constructor that says the text does not decide).
-- Months are counted as in fork F-1: a period of 3 months ending with the 15th starts on the 16th three months earlier.

§ `The assessment: descriptors, points and levels (Part 2)`

§§ `How many points do I score for an activity (reg 7(1))`

-- Priya (washing and bathing): over a year, 4d (2 points) applies on 265 of 365 days and 4a on 100. 265 is over half of 365, so 4d applies: 2 points.
#ASSERT `How many points do I score for this activity` `daily living activity 4, washing and bathing` `letter d` 265 `letter a` 100 `letter b` 0 365 EQUALS JUST 2
-- Owen (preparing food): 1b (2 points) on 300 days and 1e (4 points) on 250 days, each over half of 365: reg 7(1)(b), the higher score, 4.
#ASSERT `How many points do I score for this activity` `daily living activity 1, preparing food` `letter b` 300 `letter e` 250 `letter a` 0 365 EQUALS JUST 4
-- Lena (dressing): 6b (2 points) on 150 days and 6e (4 points) on 100 days; neither is over half but together 250 is, so reg 7(1)(c)(i): the one satisfied for more days, 6b, 2 points.
#ASSERT `How many points do I score for this activity` `daily living activity 6, dressing and undressing` `letter b` 150 `letter e` 100 `letter a` 0 365 EQUALS JUST 2
-- Lena after a bad winter: 6b 120 days and 6e 120 days (240 together, over half): the same proportion, so reg 7(1)(c)(ii): the higher score, 6e, 4 points.
#ASSERT `How many points do I score for this activity` `daily living activity 6, dressing and undressing` `letter b` 120 `letter e` 120 `letter a` 0 365 EQUALS JUST 4
-- Boundary of "over 50%" in a 365 day period: 183 days is over half (182.5), 2 points for 10b.
#ASSERT `How many points do I score for this activity` `daily living activity 10, making budgeting decisions` `letter b` 183 `letter a` 0 `letter c` 0 365 EQUALS JUST 2
-- Boundary, other side: 182 days is not over half, and one descriptor alone cannot be added to anything: no descriptor applies. Not covered (fork F-7).
#ASSERT `How many points do I score for this activity` `daily living activity 10, making budgeting decisions` `letter b` 182 `letter a` 0 `letter c` 0 365 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A 0 point descriptor does not count towards the added days of reg 7(1)(c): 9a (0 points) 100 days and 9b (2 points) 90 days; only one scoring descriptor, so none applies. Not covered.
#ASSERT `How many points do I score for this activity` `daily living activity 9, engaging with other people face to face` `letter a` 100 `letter b` 90 `letter c` 0 365 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A required period of 364 days (a claim after an interval): 183 days is over half of 364 (182), 2 points for 10b.
#ASSERT `How many points do I score for this activity` `daily living activity 10, making budgeting decisions` `letter b` 183 `letter a` 0 `letter c` 0 364 EQUALS JUST 2
-- Exactly half of 364 (182 days) is not over 50%: no descriptor applies.
#ASSERT `How many points do I score for this activity` `daily living activity 10, making budgeting decisions` `letter b` 182 `letter a` 0 `letter c` 0 364 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Mobility: Asha cannot follow a familiar journey without another person on 330 days (1f, 12 points).
#ASSERT `How many points do I score for this activity` `mobility activity 1, planning and following journeys` `letter f` 330 `letter a` 35 `letter b` 0 365 EQUALS JUST 12
-- Mobility: Kofi can stand and move more than 50 but no more than 200 metres on 250 days (2b, 4 points).
#ASSERT `How many points do I score for this activity` `mobility activity 2, moving around` `letter b` 250 `letter a` 115 `letter c` 0 365 EQUALS JUST 4
-- Not covered: moving around has descriptors a to f only; letter g names none, and 300 days are given for it, so the question does not score the activity from the other descriptors alone.
#ASSERT `How many points do I score for this activity` `mobility activity 2, moving around` `letter g` 300 `letter a` 0 `letter b` 0 365 EQUALS NOTHING
-- The same where a real descriptor (10b, 2 points) is satisfied on 300 days and a letter that names none has 10 days: still not scored.
#ASSERT `How many points do I score for this activity` `daily living activity 10, making budgeting decisions` `letter b` 300 `letter g` 10 `letter a` 0 365 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A letter that names no descriptor with no days given is padding and changes nothing: 10b on 300 days is 2 points.
#ASSERT `How many points do I score for this activity` `daily living activity 10, making budgeting decisions` `letter b` 300 `letter g` 0 `letter a` 0 365 EQUALS JUST 2

§§ `What is my score for daily living activities (reg 5(1), (2))`

-- Maria (arthritis): 1b 2, 2a 0, 3b 1, 4c 2, 5a 0, 6b 2, 7a 0, 8a 0, 9a 0, 10a 0: 7 points.
#ASSERT `What is my score for daily living activities` `daily living 1b` `daily living 2a` `daily living 3b` `daily living 4c` `daily living 5a` `daily living 6b` `daily living 7a` `daily living 8a` `daily living 9a` `daily living 10a` EQUALS JUST 7
-- Dev (severe anxiety and OCD): 1d 2, 2d 4, 3d 4, 4e 3, 5c 2, 6c 2, 7a 0, 8a 0, 9d 8, 10c 4: 29 points.
#ASSERT `What is my score for daily living activities` `daily living 1d` `daily living 2d` `daily living 3d` `daily living 4e` `daily living 5c` `daily living 6c` `daily living 7a` `daily living 8a` `daily living 9d` `daily living 10c` EQUALS JUST 29
-- Nobody needs help: every a descriptor, 0 points.
#ASSERT `What is my score for daily living activities` `daily living 1a` `daily living 2a` `daily living 3a` `daily living 4a` `daily living 5a` `daily living 6a` `daily living 7a` `daily living 8a` `daily living 9a` `daily living 10a` EQUALS JUST 0
-- The highest descriptor of each activity: 8 + 10 + 8 + 8 + 8 + 8 + 12 + 8 + 8 + 6 = 84.
#ASSERT `What is my score for daily living activities` `daily living 1f` `daily living 2f` `daily living 3f` `daily living 4g` `daily living 5f` `daily living 6f` `daily living 7e` `daily living 8e` `daily living 9d` `daily living 10d` EQUALS JUST 84
-- Not covered: no descriptor of activity 7 (communicating verbally) applies to Sam, so the text gives no score.
#ASSERT `What is my score for daily living activities` `daily living 1a` `daily living 2a` `daily living 3a` `daily living 4a` `daily living 5a` `daily living 6a` `no descriptor of daily living activity 7 applies` `daily living 8a` `daily living 9a` `daily living 10a` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Do I have limited or severely limited ability, daily living (regs 4(1), 4(3), 5(3))`

-- Maria scored 7 after an assessment, and her difficulties come from her arthritis: neither level (7 is below 8).
#ASSERT `Do I have limited or severely limited ability to carry out daily living activities` TRUE TRUE `daily living 1b` `daily living 2a` `daily living 3b` `daily living 4c` `daily living 5a` `daily living 6b` `daily living 7a` `daily living 8a` `daily living 9a` `daily living 10a` EQUALS JUST `neither limited ability nor severely limited ability`
-- Boundary: 8 points (1f alone) is limited ability.
#ASSERT `Do I have limited or severely limited ability to carry out daily living activities` TRUE TRUE `daily living 1f` `daily living 2a` `daily living 3a` `daily living 4a` `daily living 5a` `daily living 6a` `daily living 7a` `daily living 8a` `daily living 9a` `daily living 10a` EQUALS JUST `limited ability`
-- 11 points (1f 8 + 4e 3) is still limited ability.
#ASSERT `Do I have limited or severely limited ability to carry out daily living activities` TRUE TRUE `daily living 1f` `daily living 2a` `daily living 3a` `daily living 4e` `daily living 5a` `daily living 6a` `daily living 7a` `daily living 8a` `daily living 9a` `daily living 10a` EQUALS JUST `limited ability`
-- 12 points (1f 8 + 5d 4) is severely limited ability, and reg 4(3) says not also limited.
#ASSERT `Do I have limited or severely limited ability to carry out daily living activities` TRUE TRUE `daily living 1f` `daily living 2a` `daily living 3a` `daily living 4a` `daily living 5d` `daily living 6a` `daily living 7a` `daily living 8a` `daily living 9a` `daily living 10a` EQUALS JUST `severely limited ability`
-- Dev, 29 points: severely limited.
#ASSERT `Do I have limited or severely limited ability to carry out daily living activities` TRUE TRUE `daily living 1d` `daily living 2d` `daily living 3d` `daily living 4e` `daily living 5c` `daily living 6c` `daily living 7a` `daily living 8a` `daily living 9d` `daily living 10c` EQUALS JUST `severely limited ability`
-- Dev's difficulties do not result from a physical or mental condition (reg 4(1) asks that they do): neither level.
#ASSERT `Do I have limited or severely limited ability to carry out daily living activities` TRUE FALSE `daily living 1d` `daily living 2d` `daily living 3d` `daily living 4e` `daily living 5c` `daily living 6c` `daily living 7a` `daily living 8a` `daily living 9d` `daily living 10c` EQUALS JUST `neither limited ability nor severely limited ability`
-- Not covered: Maria has not undergone an assessment (regs 5(3) and 6(3) apply where C has undergone one), so the text gives no level.
#ASSERT `Do I have limited or severely limited ability to carry out daily living activities` FALSE TRUE `daily living 1b` `daily living 2a` `daily living 3b` `daily living 4c` `daily living 5a` `daily living 6b` `daily living 7a` `daily living 8a` `daily living 9a` `daily living 10a` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Mobility score and level (regs 4(1), 6(1) to (3))`

-- Hana needs prompting to undertake a journey (1b, 4 points) and can move more than 200 metres (2a, 0): 4 points.
#ASSERT `What is my score for mobility activities` `mobility 1b` `mobility 2a` EQUALS JUST 4
-- Jun cannot follow an unfamiliar journey alone (1d, 10) and can move 20 to 50 metres unaided (2c, 8): 18 points.
#ASSERT `What is my score for mobility activities` `mobility 1d` `mobility 2c` EQUALS JUST 18
-- No descriptor of moving around applies: not covered.
#ASSERT `What is my score for mobility activities` `mobility 1a` `no descriptor of mobility activity 2 applies` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 4 points after an assessment: neither level.
#ASSERT `Do I have limited or severely limited ability to carry out mobility activities` TRUE TRUE `mobility 1b` `mobility 2a` EQUALS JUST `neither limited ability nor severely limited ability`
-- 8 points (1c alone) is limited ability: the boundary.
#ASSERT `Do I have limited or severely limited ability to carry out mobility activities` TRUE TRUE `mobility 1c` `mobility 2a` EQUALS JUST `limited ability`
-- 8 points as 4 + 4 (1b and 2b) is the same.
#ASSERT `Do I have limited or severely limited ability to carry out mobility activities` TRUE TRUE `mobility 1b` `mobility 2b` EQUALS JUST `limited ability`
-- 10 points (2d alone) is limited ability, below 12.
#ASSERT `Do I have limited or severely limited ability to carry out mobility activities` TRUE TRUE `mobility 1a` `mobility 2d` EQUALS JUST `limited ability`
-- 12 points (2e alone) is severely limited ability: the boundary.
#ASSERT `Do I have limited or severely limited ability to carry out mobility activities` TRUE TRUE `mobility 1a` `mobility 2e` EQUALS JUST `severely limited ability`
-- Not covered: no assessment, no level.
#ASSERT `Do I have limited or severely limited ability to carry out mobility activities` FALSE TRUE `mobility 1a` `mobility 2e` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Doing an activity safely, to a standard, repeatedly and in reasonable time; aids (reg 4(2), (2A), (4))`

-- Tariq can do it safely, to an acceptable standard, 5 times of the 5 reasonably required, in 20 minutes where a person without his condition takes 10: twice as long is the most allowed, so he may be assessed as satisfying the descriptor.
#ASSERT `Can I be assessed as satisfying a descriptor that turns on doing an activity` FALSE FALSE TRUE 5 5 20 10
-- 21 minutes against 10 is more than twice as long.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I be assessed as satisfying a descriptor that turns on doing an activity` FALSE FALSE TRUE 5 5 21 10)
-- He can complete it only 4 times of the 5 reasonably required: not repeatedly.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I be assessed as satisfying a descriptor that turns on doing an activity` FALSE FALSE TRUE 4 5 20 10)
-- Doing it is likely to cause him harm afterwards: not safely.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I be assessed as satisfying a descriptor that turns on doing an activity` TRUE FALSE TRUE 5 5 20 10)
-- Doing it is likely to cause harm to another person: not safely.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I be assessed as satisfying a descriptor that turns on doing an activity` FALSE TRUE TRUE 5 5 20 10)
-- He cannot do it to an acceptable standard.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I be assessed as satisfying a descriptor that turns on doing an activity` FALSE FALSE FALSE 5 5 20 10)
-- Reg 4(2): the aid she normally uses (a walking frame) is taken into account.
#ASSERT `Is an aid or appliance taken into account when I am assessed` TRUE FALSE
-- Reg 4(2): an aid she does not use but could reasonably be expected to use is taken into account too (limb (b)).
#ASSERT `Is an aid or appliance taken into account when I am assessed` FALSE TRUE
-- An aid she neither uses nor could reasonably be expected to use is not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is an aid or appliance taken into account when I am assessed` FALSE FALSE)

§§ `How many days are in my required period (reg 7(3))`

-- Reg 7(3)(a)(i): Imogen's previous award ended on 15 December 2023 and she claims again on 1 March 2024. The 3 months ending 15 December 2023 start on 16 September 2023 (91 days: 15 + 31 + 30 + 15), and the 9 months beginning 1 March 2024 end on 30 November 2024 (275 days): 366 days.
#ASSERT `How many days are in my required period` `a claim made after an interval, under regulation 15 or 15A` (YMD 2023 12 15) (YMD 2024 3 1) (YMD 2024 3 1) EQUALS 366
-- Reg 7(3)(a)(ii): an ordinary claim with a prescribed date of 15 June 2025. The 3 months ending 15 June start on 16 March (92 days: 16 + 30 + 31 + 15), and the 9 months beginning 16 June end on 15 March 2026 (273 days): 365 days.
#ASSERT `How many days are in my required period` `any other claim` (YMD 2025 6 15) (YMD 2025 6 20) (YMD 2025 6 15) EQUALS 365
-- Reg 7(3)(b)(i): a day of the award, 15 August 2025, in the 3 months after a claim for the purpose of regulation 15 (prescribed date 15 June 2025). 92 days for the 3 months, and the 9 months beginning 16 August 2025 end on 15 May 2026 (273 days): 365 days.
#ASSERT `How many days are in my required period` `a day of my award in the 3 months after such a claim` (YMD 2025 6 15) (YMD 2025 6 20) (YMD 2025 8 15) EQUALS 365
-- Reg 7(3)(b)(ii): any other day of an award, 15 February 2024. The 3 months ending 15 February 2024 start on 16 November 2023 (92 days: 15 + 31 + 31 + 15), and the 9 months beginning 16 February 2024 end on 15 November 2024 (274 days, 2024 being a leap year): 366 days.
#ASSERT `How many days are in my required period` `a day of my award in any other case` (YMD 2024 2 15) (YMD 2024 2 15) (YMD 2024 2 15) EQUALS 366

§§ `Information and evidence I am asked for (reg 8(2), (3), reg 10)`

-- Reg 8(2): Nadia is asked on 10 March 2025 for medical evidence; she has one month, to 10 April 2025.
#ASSERT `By what day must I give the information or evidence` (YMD 2025 3 10) FALSE (YMD 2025 3 10) EQUALS (YMD 2025 4 10)
-- The Secretary of State allows her until 1 May 2025, a longer period it considers reasonable: that is the last day.
#ASSERT `By what day must I give the information or evidence` (YMD 2025 3 10) TRUE (YMD 2025 5 1) EQUALS (YMD 2025 5 1)
-- A "longer period" that ends before the month is out (20 March) gives her nothing: the month stands (fork F-1).
#ASSERT `By what day must I give the information or evidence` (YMD 2025 3 10) TRUE (YMD 2025 3 20) EQUALS (YMD 2025 4 10)
-- Asked on 31 January 2025: one month on is 28 February 2025 (fork F-1, asserted).
#ASSERT `By what day must I give the information or evidence` (YMD 2025 1 31) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 31) EQUALS (YMD 2025 2 28)
-- Reg 8(3): she does not provide it and has no good reason: a negative determination must be made.
#ASSERT `Must a negative determination be made against me for not giving the information or evidence in time` (YMD 2025 3 10) FALSE (YMD 2025 3 10) FALSE (YMD 2025 3 10) FALSE
-- She provides it on 10 April, the last day: in time, no negative determination.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must a negative determination be made against me for not giving the information or evidence in time` (YMD 2025 3 10) FALSE (YMD 2025 3 10) TRUE (YMD 2025 4 10) FALSE)
-- She provides it on 11 April, a day late, with no good reason: a negative determination must be made.
#ASSERT `Must a negative determination be made against me for not giving the information or evidence in time` (YMD 2025 3 10) FALSE (YMD 2025 3 10) TRUE (YMD 2025 4 11) FALSE
-- A day late, but the Secretary of State is satisfied she had good reason (she was in hospital, reg 10): none.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must a negative determination be made against me for not giving the information or evidence in time` (YMD 2025 3 10) FALSE (YMD 2025 3 10) TRUE (YMD 2025 4 11) TRUE)
-- Reg 10: her state of health at the relevant time must be taken into account in deciding good reason.
#ASSERT `Must the Secretary of State take this matter into account` `C's state of health at the relevant time`
-- Reg 10: so must the nature of any disability she has.
#ASSERT `Must the Secretary of State take this matter into account` `the nature of any disability that C has`

§§ `Missing a consultation (reg 9)`

-- Reg 9: Colm misses a telephone consultation with an approved person, has no good reason, and was sent 7 days written notice (sent 1 March for 8 March): a negative determination must be made.
#ASSERT `Must a negative determination be made against me for missing a consultation` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 3 8) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Only 6 days' written notice (sent 1 March for 7 March) and he did not agree to shorter notice: reg 9(3) is not met, no negative determination.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must a negative determination be made against me for missing a consultation` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 3 7) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The same 6 days' notice, but he agreed to accept shorter notice: reg 9(2) applies.
#ASSERT `Must a negative determination be made against me for missing a consultation` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 3 7) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- The notice was an email and he had not agreed to correspondence by electronic communication: not written notice under reg 9(4).
#ASSERT NOT (`Must a negative determination be made against me for missing a consultation` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 3 8) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- An email notice, 7 days, where he had agreed to accept correspondence that way: written notice.
#ASSERT `Must a negative determination be made against me for missing a consultation` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 3 8) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- The consultation was not with a person approved by the Secretary of State (reg 9(5)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Must a negative determination be made against me for missing a consultation` FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 3 8) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- He attended: reg 9(2) does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must a negative determination be made against me for missing a consultation` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 3 8) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- He missed it with good reason: reg 9(2) does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must a negative determination be made against me for missing a consultation` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 3 8) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `A fresh look at my ability (reg 11)`

-- Reg 11(1): Ruth has been found to have limited ability; the Secretary of State may look afresh for any reason, here a letter from her GP.
#ASSERT `May the Secretary of State look at my ability afresh for this reason` TRUE `any other reason`
-- Reg 11(2): doing work for payment is not a reason.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Secretary of State look at my ability afresh for this reason` TRUE `C is doing work for payment or in expectation of payment`)
-- Reg 11(2): nor is voluntary work.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Secretary of State look at my ability afresh for this reason` TRUE `C is doing voluntary work`)
-- Reg 11(1) needs an earlier determination: before one, there is nothing to determine afresh.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Secretary of State look at my ability afresh for this reason` FALSE `any other reason`)

§ `The required period condition (Part 3)`

§§ `Which rate do I meet the required period condition for (regs 12, 13)`

-- Reg 12(1): Salma is likely to be found to have limited ability in daily living for all of the 3 months to her prescribed date and all of the 9 months after: the standard rate.
#ASSERT `Which rate of the daily living component do I meet the required period condition for` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the standard rate of the component`
-- Reg 12(2): severely limited ability throughout both windows: the enhanced rate.
#ASSERT `Which rate of the daily living component do I meet the required period condition for` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the enhanced rate of the component`
-- Limited ability in the 3 months to the prescribed date but not the 9 months after (her condition is expected to improve): neither rate.
#ASSERT `Which rate of the daily living component do I meet the required period condition for` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no rate of the component`
-- Limited ability for the 9 months after but not the 3 months before (recent onset): neither rate.
#ASSERT `Which rate of the daily living component do I meet the required period condition for` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no rate of the component`
-- Reg 15A(4) or 15B(4) regards the look-back as met: limited ability for the next 9 months suffices for the standard rate.
#ASSERT `Which rate of the daily living component do I meet the required period condition for` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the standard rate of the component`
-- The same, with severely limited ability for the next 9 months: the enhanced rate.
#ASSERT `Which rate of the daily living component do I meet the required period condition for` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the enhanced rate of the component`
-- The look-back is regarded as met but nothing is expected for the next 9 months: no rate.
#ASSERT `Which rate of the daily living component do I meet the required period condition for` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no rate of the component`
-- Reg 13(1): the mobility component at the standard rate.
#ASSERT `Which rate of the mobility component do I meet the required period condition for` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the standard rate of the component`
-- Reg 13(2): the mobility component at the enhanced rate.
#ASSERT `Which rate of the mobility component do I meet the required period condition for` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the enhanced rate of the component`
-- Reg 13: no mobility rate where the 9 months after fail.
#ASSERT `Which rate of the mobility component do I meet the required period condition for` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no rate of the component`
-- Reg 15B(4): look-back regarded as met, severely limited ability expected: the enhanced rate of mobility.
#ASSERT `Which rate of the mobility component do I meet the required period condition for` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the enhanced rate of the component`

§§ `What is my prescribed date (reg 14)`

-- Reg 14(b): Joel has an award; for the day of it, 15 August 2025, the prescribed date is that day.
#ASSERT `What is my prescribed date` TRUE (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 2025 3 10) FALSE (YMD 2025 3 10) EQUALS (YMD 2025 8 15)
-- Reg 14(a): Joel claimed on 10 March 2025 and has no award; had he been assessed at every time in the previous 3 months it would not be likely that he would have had limited ability: no date; the date of the claim (fork F-13).
#ASSERT `What is my prescribed date` FALSE (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 2025 3 10) FALSE (YMD 2025 3 10) EQUALS (YMD 2025 3 10)
-- Reg 14(a): the earliest date from which it is likely he would have been found limited is 1 May 2025, later than the claim: that later date.
#ASSERT `What is my prescribed date` FALSE (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 2025 3 10) TRUE (YMD 2025 5 1) EQUALS (YMD 2025 5 1)
-- Reg 14(a): that date is 1 February 2025, before the claim: "if later", so the date of the claim.
#ASSERT `What is my prescribed date` FALSE (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 2025 3 10) TRUE (YMD 2025 2 1) EQUALS (YMD 2025 3 10)

§§ `A new claim after an earlier award (regs 15, 15A, 15B)`

-- Reg 15(1): Wanjiru's personal independence payment ended on 15 June 2024; she claims on 15 June 2025 (1 year later), same component, same condition: reg 15 applies.
#ASSERT `Do I have a claim after an interval under regulation 15` `personal independence payment` (YMD 2024 6 15) (YMD 2025 6 15) FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Boundary: an award that ended exactly 2 years before the claim (15 June 2023 to 15 June 2025) is "not more than 2 years" before (fork F-15).
#ASSERT `Do I have a claim after an interval under regulation 15` `personal independence payment` (YMD 2023 6 15) (YMD 2025 6 15) FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Boundary, other side: ended 14 June 2023, more than 2 years before 15 June 2025.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a claim after an interval under regulation 15` `personal independence payment` (YMD 2023 6 14) (YMD 2025 6 15) FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- An adult disability payment award counts as well.
#ASSERT `Do I have a claim after an interval under regulation 15` `adult disability payment` (YMD 2024 6 15) (YMD 2025 6 15) FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- A disability living allowance award is not named in reg 15(1)(b).
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a claim after an interval under regulation 15` `disability living allowance` (YMD 2024 6 15) (YMD 2025 6 15) FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- Reg 26(2)(b): once she has reached the relevant age, "2 years" is read "1 year": an award that ended exactly 1 year before still counts.
#ASSERT `Do I have a claim after an interval under regulation 15` `personal independence payment` (YMD 2024 6 15) (YMD 2025 6 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Reg 26(2)(b): a day more than 1 year before does not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a claim after an interval under regulation 15` `personal independence payment` (YMD 2024 6 14) (YMD 2025 6 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- The previous award was not of the component she now claims (reg 15(1)(c)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a claim after an interval under regulation 15` `personal independence payment` (YMD 2024 6 15) (YMD 2025 6 15) FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- The Secretary of State does not determine that the entitlement results from the same condition (reg 15(1)(d)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a claim after an interval under regulation 15` `personal independence payment` (YMD 2024 6 15) (YMD 2025 6 15) FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Reg 15A(1): Mia's child disability payment ended on 1 April 2025; she turned 16 on 1 September 2024 (born 1 September 2008) and claims on 1 May 2025: reg 15A applies.
#ASSERT `Do I have a claim after child disability payment under regulation 15A` `child disability payment` (YMD 2025 4 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) (YMD 2008 9 1) FALSE
-- Reg 15A(1)(c): she is 15 on the day of the claim (born 1 September 2009).
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a claim after child disability payment under regulation 15A` `child disability payment` (YMD 2025 4 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) (YMD 2009 9 1) FALSE)
-- Reg 15A(1)(c): exactly 16 on the day of the claim (born 1 May 2009) is "aged 16 years or over".
#ASSERT `Do I have a claim after child disability payment under regulation 15A` `child disability payment` (YMD 2025 4 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) (YMD 2009 5 1) FALSE
-- Reg 15A(1)(b): the award ended exactly 2 years before the claim (1 May 2023): not more than 2 years.
#ASSERT `Do I have a claim after child disability payment under regulation 15A` `child disability payment` (YMD 2023 5 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) (YMD 2008 9 1) FALSE
-- The award ended on 30 April 2023, more than 2 years before the claim.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a claim after child disability payment under regulation 15A` `child disability payment` (YMD 2023 4 30) (YMD 2025 5 1) (YMD 2008 9 1) FALSE)
-- Reg 15A(5): she claims within the 13 week period of the Scottish regulations, so the award is treated as ending just before the claim; reg 15A applies.
#ASSERT `Do I have a claim after child disability payment under regulation 15A` `child disability payment` (YMD 2025 4 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) (YMD 2008 9 1) TRUE
-- The previous award was adult disability payment, not child disability payment.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a claim after child disability payment under regulation 15A` `adult disability payment` (YMD 2025 4 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) (YMD 2008 9 1) FALSE)
-- Reg 15B(1): Gareth (born 1 January 1970) had Scottish adult disability living allowance that ended on 1 March 2025; he claims on 1 May 2025, has not had personal independence payment since: reg 15B applies.
#ASSERT `Do I have a claim after Scottish adult disability living allowance under regulation 15B` `Scottish adult disability living allowance` (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) FALSE FALSE (YMD 1970 1 1) FALSE
-- Reg 15B(1)(d): born 9 April 1948 he was 64 on 8 April 2013 ("64 years old or younger"): reg 15B applies.
#ASSERT `Do I have a claim after Scottish adult disability living allowance under regulation 15B` `Scottish adult disability living allowance` (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) FALSE FALSE (YMD 1948 4 9) FALSE
-- Born 8 April 1948 he turned 65 on 8 April 2013: not 64 or younger on that day.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a claim after Scottish adult disability living allowance under regulation 15B` `Scottish adult disability living allowance` (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) FALSE FALSE (YMD 1948 4 8) FALSE)
-- Reg 15B(1)(c): he has been entitled to personal independence payment on a day since the award ended.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a claim after Scottish adult disability living allowance under regulation 15B` `Scottish adult disability living allowance` (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) FALSE TRUE (YMD 1970 1 1) FALSE)
-- Reg 26A(2)(b): having reached the relevant age, "2 years" is read "1 year": ended exactly one year before the claim is within it.
#ASSERT `Do I have a claim after Scottish adult disability living allowance under regulation 15B` `Scottish adult disability living allowance` (YMD 2024 5 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) TRUE FALSE (YMD 1950 1 1) FALSE
-- Ended 30 April 2024: more than 1 year before 1 May 2025.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a claim after Scottish adult disability living allowance under regulation 15B` `Scottish adult disability living allowance` (YMD 2024 4 30) (YMD 2025 5 1) TRUE FALSE (YMD 1950 1 1) FALSE)
-- Reg 15B(6): a claim within the 13 week period of the 2025 Regulations treats the award as ending just before the claim.
#ASSERT `Do I have a claim after Scottish adult disability living allowance under regulation 15B` `Scottish adult disability living allowance` (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) FALSE FALSE (YMD 1970 1 1) TRUE
-- The previous benefit was personal independence payment, not Scottish adult disability living allowance.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have a claim after Scottish adult disability living allowance under regulation 15B` `personal independence payment` (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) FALSE FALSE (YMD 1970 1 1) FALSE)
-- Regs 15A(4), 15B(4): either regulation applies, the look-back is regarded as met.
#ASSERT `Does my previous award mean my look-back is treated as met` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my previous award mean my look-back is treated as met` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my previous award mean my look-back is treated as met` FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Which regulation sets my dates, and from when the windows run (regs 14 to 15B)`

-- No claim after an interval: reg 14 sets the prescribed date.
#ASSERT `Which regulation sets the dates my required period condition is tested at` FALSE FALSE FALSE `determining entitlement under the new claim` EQUALS `regulation 14, there being no claim after an interval`
-- Reg 15 applies, determining entitlement under the new claim: reg 15(2).
#ASSERT `Which regulation sets the dates my required period condition is tested at` TRUE FALSE FALSE `determining entitlement under the new claim` EQUALS `regulation 15(2)`
-- Reg 15 applies, the 3 months following the new claim: reg 15(3).
#ASSERT `Which regulation sets the dates my required period condition is tested at` TRUE FALSE FALSE `continued entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim` EQUALS `regulation 15(3)`
-- Reg 15A: paragraphs (2) and (3).
#ASSERT `Which regulation sets the dates my required period condition is tested at` FALSE TRUE FALSE `determining entitlement under the new claim` EQUALS `regulation 15A(2)`
#ASSERT `Which regulation sets the dates my required period condition is tested at` FALSE TRUE FALSE `continued entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim` EQUALS `regulation 15A(3)`
-- Reg 15B: paragraphs (2) and (3).
#ASSERT `Which regulation sets the dates my required period condition is tested at` FALSE FALSE TRUE `determining entitlement under the new claim` EQUALS `regulation 15B(2)`
#ASSERT `Which regulation sets the dates my required period condition is tested at` FALSE FALSE TRUE `continued entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim` EQUALS `regulation 15B(3)`
-- Not covered: a claim that meets the conditions of both reg 15 and reg 15A (fork F-14): the text does not say which prevails.
#ASSERT `Which regulation sets the dates my required period condition is tested at` TRUE TRUE FALSE `determining entitlement under the new claim` EQUALS `more than one of regulations 15, 15A and 15B applies, and the text does not say which prevails`
-- The same for 15A and 15B together.
#ASSERT `Which regulation sets the dates my required period condition is tested at` FALSE TRUE TRUE `continued entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim` EQUALS `more than one of regulations 15, 15A and 15B applies, and the text does not say which prevails`
-- Reg 14: the 3 months look back from the prescribed date, 15 June 2025, and the 9 months run after it.
#ASSERT `From which day does my 3-month look-back run` `regulation 14, there being no claim after an interval` (YMD 2025 6 15) (YMD 2024 12 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) (YMD 2025 8 15) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 6 15)
#ASSERT `After which day do my 9 months run` `regulation 14, there being no claim after an interval` (YMD 2025 6 15) (YMD 2024 12 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) (YMD 2025 8 15) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 6 15)
-- Reg 15(2): the previous award ended 1 December 2024, the new claim is made 1 May 2025: the 3 months look back from the end of the award and the 9 months run from the claim.
#ASSERT `From which day does my 3-month look-back run` `regulation 15(2)` (YMD 2025 6 15) (YMD 2024 12 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) (YMD 2025 8 15) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2024 12 1)
#ASSERT `After which day do my 9 months run` `regulation 15(2)` (YMD 2025 6 15) (YMD 2024 12 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) (YMD 2025 8 15) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 5 1)
-- Reg 15(3): for a day of the award, 15 August 2025, the look-back still runs from the end of the previous award and the 9 months run from the day of the award.
#ASSERT `From which day does my 3-month look-back run` `regulation 15(3)` (YMD 2025 6 15) (YMD 2024 12 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) (YMD 2025 8 15) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2024 12 1)
#ASSERT `After which day do my 9 months run` `regulation 15(3)` (YMD 2025 6 15) (YMD 2024 12 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) (YMD 2025 8 15) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 8 15)
-- Reg 15A(2) and 15B(2) work the same way.
#ASSERT `From which day does my 3-month look-back run` `regulation 15A(2)` (YMD 2025 6 15) (YMD 2025 4 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) (YMD 2025 8 15) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 4 1)
#ASSERT `After which day do my 9 months run` `regulation 15B(3)` (YMD 2025 6 15) (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) (YMD 2025 8 15) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 8 15)
-- Not covered: where more than one of regs 15, 15A and 15B applies there are no dates.
#ASSERT `From which day does my 3-month look-back run` `more than one of regulations 15, 15A and 15B applies, and the text does not say which prevails` (YMD 2025 6 15) (YMD 2024 12 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) (YMD 2025 8 15) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `After which day do my 9 months run` `more than one of regulations 15, 15A and 15B applies, and the text does not say which prevails` (YMD 2025 6 15) (YMD 2024 12 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) (YMD 2025 8 15) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Residence and presence (Part 4)`

§§ `Am I present in England and Wales on this day, or treated as present (reg 16(a))`

-- Cerys lives in Cardiff and is there on the day: present in England and Wales.
#ASSERT `Am I present in England and Wales on this day, or treated as present` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Euan is in Glasgow and nothing treats him as present in England and Wales.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I present in England and Wales on this day, or treated as present` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Euan's ongoing claim must be decided under reg 23ZC(5), where reg 16(a) is read "Great Britain" (reg 23ZC(6)): present in Great Britain is enough.
#ASSERT `Am I present in England and Wales on this day, or treated as present` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Abroad on a short trip and treated as present by regs 17 to 19.
#ASSERT `Am I present in England and Wales on this day, or treated as present` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- In Scotland temporarily and treated as present by reg 20A.
#ASSERT `Am I present in England and Wales on this day, or treated as present` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Moved to Scotland and in the run-on period (reg 23ZB(2) or 23ZC(7)).
#ASSERT `Am I present in England and Wales on this day, or treated as present` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Abroad and nothing treats the person as present.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I present in England and Wales on this day, or treated as present` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Absence from Great Britain (regs 17 to 19)`

-- Reg 17: Bea is abroad on a holiday expected to last 6 weeks (unlikely to exceed 52 weeks: temporarily absent); in week 13 she is still treated as present.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as present on this day of my absence` 13 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- In week 14 she is not (the first 13 weeks only).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as present on this day of my absence` 14 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Not temporarily absent (her absence was likely to exceed 52 weeks at the start): reg 17 does not reach her even in week 1.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as present on this day of my absence` 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 18: Bea has treatment arranged abroad for a condition that began before she left, by a qualified person: 26 weeks.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as present on this day of my absence` 26 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Week 27 is beyond reg 18 and reg 18B.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as present on this day of my absence` 27 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- If the treatment is not by a qualified person, reg 18 does not apply and only 13 weeks run: week 26 is not covered.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as present on this day of my absence` 26 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 18A: Bea was in a country when the Government advised nationals to leave, the Secretary of State is satisfied it is unreasonable to expect her to return, and she did not go there after the advice: 26 weeks.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as present on this day of my absence` 20 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Reg 18A, week 27: beyond the 26 weeks.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as present on this day of my absence` 27 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Reg 18A(1)(b): the Secretary of State is not satisfied it is unreasonable to expect her to return, so only 13 weeks: week 20 is not covered.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as present on this day of my absence` 20 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Reg 18C: the same, where it is the Scottish Ministers who are satisfied.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as present on this day of my absence` 26 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Reg 18C, week 27.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as present on this day of my absence` 27 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Reg 19(1): Bea is abroad as a mariner for 100 weeks; the limit does not apply.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as present on this day of my absence` 100 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Weeks of an absence that count (reg 16(b)): a 40 week absence on holiday counts 13 weeks.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of my absence count as weeks I was present in Great Britain` 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 13
-- A 10 week absence on holiday counts all 10 (less than the 13 week limit).
#ASSERT `How many weeks of my absence count as weeks I was present in Great Britain` 10 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 10
-- A 40 week absence for medical treatment counts 26 weeks.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of my absence count as weeks I was present in Great Britain` 40 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 26
-- A 40 week absence that was not temporary counts none.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of my absence count as weeks I was present in Great Britain` 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- A 40 week absence as a mariner (reg 19(1)) counts all 40 weeks.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of my absence count as weeks I was present in Great Britain` 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 40
-- A 40 week absence after the Government advised leaving (reg 18A) counts 26 weeks.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of my absence count as weeks I was present in Great Britain` 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS 26
-- Reg 16(b): Colin was in Great Britain for 104 of the last 156 weeks: the minimum.
#ASSERT `Have I been present in Great Britain for 104 of the last 156 weeks` 104 0
-- 103 weeks is one short.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I been present in Great Britain for 104 of the last 156 weeks` 103 0)
-- Weeks treated as present count towards 104 (fork F-27): 100 present + 4 treated.
#ASSERT `Have I been present in Great Britain for 104 of the last 156 weeks` 100 4
-- 90 present + 13 treated is 103.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I been present in Great Britain for 104 of the last 156 weeks` 90 13)

§§ `Habitual residence and immigration control (reg 16(c), (d))`

-- Reg 16(c): Fatima, living in the United Kingdom, is habitually resident in the places the paragraph names.
#ASSERT `Am I habitually resident in a place that satisfies regulation 16(c)` `the daily living component` `the United Kingdom` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Republic of Ireland is named too.
#ASSERT `Am I habitually resident in a place that satisfies regulation 16(c)` `the daily living component` `the Republic of Ireland` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Switzerland is not named.
#ASSERT `Am I habitually resident in a place that satisfies regulation 16(c)` `the daily living component` `Switzerland` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Reg 20: a person living in Spain as a soldier's spouse is treated as habitually resident in Great Britain.
#ASSERT `Am I habitually resident in a place that satisfies regulation 16(c)` `the daily living component` `some other place` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Reg 23 sets 16(a) to (c) aside for the daily living component of someone living in an EEA state...
#ASSERT `Am I habitually resident in a place that satisfies regulation 16(c)` `the daily living component` `an EEA state other than the Republic of Ireland` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- ... but not for the mobility component.
#ASSERT `Am I habitually resident in a place that satisfies regulation 16(c)` `the mobility component` `an EEA state other than the Republic of Ireland` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Reg 23A(1A): a person with refugee leave who lives elsewhere is not tested on 16(c).
#ASSERT `Am I habitually resident in a place that satisfies regulation 16(c)` `the mobility component` `some other place` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Reg 23ZA: someone who moved from Scotland within 13 weeks is treated as not satisfying 16(c), even living in the United Kingdom.
#ASSERT `Am I habitually resident in a place that satisfies regulation 16(c)` `the daily living component` `the United Kingdom` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered: reg 23ZA says "not satisfied" and reg 20 deems it satisfied; the text does not say which prevails (fork F-22).
#ASSERT `Am I habitually resident in a place that satisfies regulation 16(c)` `the daily living component` `some other place` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not covered: reg 23ZA and reg 23A(1A).
#ASSERT `Am I habitually resident in a place that satisfies regulation 16(c)` `the daily living component` `the United Kingdom` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Reg 16(d)(i): not subject to immigration control.
#ASSERT `Am I a person who is not excluded by immigration control` TRUE FALSE
-- Reg 16(d)(ii): subject to control but section 115 does not apply for this benefit.
#ASSERT `Am I a person who is not excluded by immigration control` FALSE TRUE
-- Neither.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a person who is not excluded by immigration control` FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Do I meet regulation 16 on this day`

-- Ordinary case: present, 104 weeks, in the United Kingdom, not subject to immigration control.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence and presence conditions of regulation 16 on this day` `the daily living component` TRUE TRUE `the United Kingdom` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the conditions of regulation 16 are met`
-- Only 90 weeks in Great Britain: 16(b) fails.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence and presence conditions of regulation 16 on this day` `the daily living component` TRUE FALSE `the United Kingdom` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the conditions of regulation 16 are not met`
-- Terminally ill (reg 21): 16(b) is omitted.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence and presence conditions of regulation 16 on this day` `the daily living component` TRUE FALSE `the United Kingdom` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the conditions of regulation 16 are met`
-- Reg 22: a relevant EU Regulation applies: 16(b) does not apply.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence and presence conditions of regulation 16 on this day` `the daily living component` TRUE FALSE `the United Kingdom` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the conditions of regulation 16 are met`
-- Reg 23A: refugee leave: 16(b) and (c) do not apply, but 16(a) and (d) do.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence and presence conditions of regulation 16 on this day` `the daily living component` TRUE FALSE `some other place` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the conditions of regulation 16 are met`
-- Reg 23A does not rescue 16(a).
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence and presence conditions of regulation 16 on this day` `the daily living component` FALSE FALSE `some other place` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the conditions of regulation 16 are not met`
-- Habitually resident in "some other place": 16(c) fails.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence and presence conditions of regulation 16 on this day` `the daily living component` TRUE TRUE `some other place` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the conditions of regulation 16 are not met`
-- Subject to immigration control and section 115 applies: 16(d) fails.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence and presence conditions of regulation 16 on this day` `the daily living component` TRUE TRUE `the United Kingdom` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the conditions of regulation 16 are not met`
-- Subject to immigration control but section 115 does not apply for this purpose: 16(d)(ii).
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence and presence conditions of regulation 16 on this day` `the daily living component` TRUE TRUE `the United Kingdom` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the conditions of regulation 16 are met`
-- Reg 23: an EEA resident's daily living component is not tested on (a) to (c), but (d) still applies.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence and presence conditions of regulation 16 on this day` `the daily living component` FALSE FALSE `an EEA state other than the Republic of Ireland` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the conditions of regulation 16 are met`
-- Reg 23: the mobility component is not helped.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence and presence conditions of regulation 16 on this day` `the mobility component` FALSE FALSE `an EEA state other than the Republic of Ireland` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the conditions of regulation 16 are not met`
-- Reg 23ZA: 16(c) treated as not satisfied for someone who moved from Scotland.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence and presence conditions of regulation 16 on this day` `the daily living component` TRUE TRUE `the United Kingdom` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the conditions of regulation 16 are not met`
-- Not covered: reg 23ZA together with reg 20 (fork F-22): the text does not say whether regulation 16 is met.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence and presence conditions of regulation 16 on this day` `the daily living component` TRUE TRUE `some other place` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the text does not say whether the conditions of regulation 16 are met`

§§ `Forces service and work abroad (regs 19, 20, Schedule 2)`

-- Reg 19(2): Sgt Okafor (born 1 January 1990) is in the regular forces, not in Schedule 2, and not a deserter.
#ASSERT `Am I a member of Her Majesty's forces for regulations 19 and 20` TRUE FALSE (YMD 1990 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 1) FALSE
-- A civilian is not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a member of Her Majesty's forces for regulations 19 and 20` FALSE FALSE (YMD 1990 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 1) FALSE)
-- A locally entered person specified in Schedule 2 is not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a member of Her Majesty's forces for regulations 19 and 20` TRUE TRUE (YMD 1990 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 1) FALSE)
-- Absent on desertion.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a member of Her Majesty's forces for regulations 19 and 20` TRUE FALSE (YMD 1990 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 1) TRUE)
-- "Over the age of 16" read strictly (fork F-19): on the 16th birthday itself (1 March 2025) a cadet is not yet over 16.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a member of Her Majesty's forces for regulations 19 and 20` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2009 3 1) (YMD 2025 3 1) FALSE)
-- The day after the 16th birthday, over 16.
#ASSERT `Am I a member of Her Majesty's forces for regulations 19 and 20` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2009 3 1) (YMD 2025 3 2) FALSE
-- Schedule 2 paragraph 1(a): a locally entered naval person who has never been insured or paid contributions is specified.
#ASSERT `Am I specified in Schedule 2` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Paragraph 2: if he has paid Class 1 contributions, paragraph 1(a) does not include him.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I specified in Schedule 2` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Paragraph 2: nor if he has been an insured person under the 1965 Act.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I specified in Schedule 2` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Paragraph 1(b): a military person recruited abroad whose unit's depot is outside the United Kingdom.
#ASSERT `Am I specified in Schedule 2` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Paragraph 1(b): the depot is in the United Kingdom.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I specified in Schedule 2` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Paragraph 1(c): an air force person recruited abroad liable to serve only in a specified part of the world outside the United Kingdom.
#ASSERT `Am I specified in Schedule 2` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Paragraph 1(c): not so liable.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I specified in Schedule 2` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- No paragraph applies.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I specified in Schedule 2` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 19(3): a pilot employed under a contract of service is an aircraft worker.
#ASSERT `Am I an aircraft worker` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A baggage handler on board employed for the aircraft's purposes under a contract made in the United Kingdom for performance in flight.
#ASSERT `Am I an aircraft worker` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- The same, under a contract made abroad: not an aircraft worker.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I an aircraft worker` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- A member of Her Majesty's forces employed on an aircraft is excluded.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I an aircraft worker` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Not employed under a contract of service.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I an aircraft worker` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 19(3): a ship's master is a mariner.
#ASSERT `Am I a mariner` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A catering worker on board in another capacity, contract made in the United Kingdom for performance on voyage.
#ASSERT `Am I a mariner` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- The same, contract made abroad.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a mariner` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- A member of the forces on a ship is excluded.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a mariner` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Reg 19(1)(a)(ii): abroad as an aircraft worker: treated as present.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as present because of my work abroad or a family member's service` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `some other relationship`
-- Reg 19(1)(b): continental shelf employment.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as present because of my work abroad or a family member's service` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `some other relationship`
-- Reg 19(1)(c): living with a soldier abroad and being the soldier's spouse.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as present because of my work abroad or a family member's service` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `spouse`
-- Reg 19(1)(c): living with the soldier as a civil partner too.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as present because of my work abroad or a family member's service` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `civil partner`
-- Reg 19(1)(c): a friend living with the soldier is not in the list.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as present because of my work abroad or a family member's service` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `some other relationship`)
-- Reg 19(1) applies where C is absent from Great Britain: a person not absent needs no treatment.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as present because of my work abroad or a family member's service` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `some other relationship`)
-- Reg 20: resident abroad in the capacity of a soldier.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as habitually resident in Great Britain because of forces service` TRUE FALSE `some other relationship`
-- Reg 20(b): living with a soldier and being the soldier's mother.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as habitually resident in Great Britain because of forces service` FALSE TRUE `mother`
-- Reg 20(b): not in the list.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as habitually resident in Great Britain because of forces service` FALSE TRUE `some other relationship`)
-- Reg 20A: Dylan lives in Wales, is in Edinburgh for a week: treated as present.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as present in England and Wales while I am in Scotland` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Reg 20A(b): he is not in Scotland (he is in France).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as present in England and Wales while I am in Scotland` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Reg 20A(a): he has moved there, not temporarily absent.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as present in England and Wales while I am in Scotland` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)

§§ `Exceptions to the 104 week test and to regulation 16(a) to (c) (regs 21 to 23A)`

-- Reg 21: Ivy is terminally ill and claims expressly on that ground: 16(b) is omitted.
#ASSERT `Is the 104-week presence test set aside because I am terminally ill` TRUE TRUE
-- Terminally ill but the claim is not made expressly on that ground.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the 104-week presence test set aside because I am terminally ill` TRUE FALSE)
-- Claims on that ground but is not terminally ill.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the 104-week presence test set aside because I am terminally ill` FALSE TRUE)
-- Reg 22: habitually resident in Great Britain, a relevant EU Regulation applies, and a genuine and sufficient link.
#ASSERT `Is the 104-week presence test set aside because a relevant EU Regulation applies to me in Great Britain` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the 104-week presence test set aside because a relevant EU Regulation applies to me in Great Britain` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the 104-week presence test set aside because a relevant EU Regulation applies to me in Great Britain` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the 104-week presence test set aside because a relevant EU Regulation applies to me in Great Britain` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Reg 23: Lars lives in Germany (an EEA state other than Ireland), a relevant EU Regulation applies to him, and he has a genuine and sufficient link.
#ASSERT `Are the presence and residence tests set aside for my daily living component because I live in an EEA state or Switzerland` `an EEA state other than the Republic of Ireland` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) TRUE
-- Anne lives in Switzerland; a relevant EU Regulation applied to her on 31 December 2020 and she has been in continuous receipt since 1 May 2019; she has not been in the United Kingdom since: reg 23(b)(ii).
#ASSERT `Are the presence and residence tests set aside for my daily living component because I live in an EEA state or Switzerland` `Switzerland` FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2019 5 1) TRUE
-- The same, but she was habitually resident in the United Kingdom on 1 June 2021 (after 31 December 2020): the exception in (b)(ii).
#ASSERT NOT (`Are the presence and residence tests set aside for my daily living component because I live in an EEA state or Switzerland` `Switzerland` FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2021 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2019 5 1) TRUE)
-- Boundary: her latest day in the United Kingdom was 31 December 2020 itself: not "after" 31 December 2020.
#ASSERT `Are the presence and residence tests set aside for my daily living component because I live in an EEA state or Switzerland` `Switzerland` FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 12 31) TRUE (YMD 2019 5 1) TRUE
-- Boundary, other side: 1 January 2021.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are the presence and residence tests set aside for my daily living component because I live in an EEA state or Switzerland` `Switzerland` FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2021 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2019 5 1) TRUE)
-- Her continuous receipt began on 31 December 2020 itself: "on and from that date".
#ASSERT `Are the presence and residence tests set aside for my daily living component because I live in an EEA state or Switzerland` `Switzerland` FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2020 12 31) TRUE
-- Her receipt began on 1 February 2021, after that date.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are the presence and residence tests set aside for my daily living component because I live in an EEA state or Switzerland` `Switzerland` FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2021 2 1) TRUE)
-- She is in the United Kingdom, not in an EEA state.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are the presence and residence tests set aside for my daily living component because I live in an EEA state or Switzerland` `the United Kingdom` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) TRUE)
-- The Republic of Ireland is an EEA state.
#ASSERT `Are the presence and residence tests set aside for my daily living component because I live in an EEA state or Switzerland` `the Republic of Ireland` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) TRUE
-- No genuine and sufficient link.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are the presence and residence tests set aside for my daily living component because I live in an EEA state or Switzerland` `Switzerland` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) FALSE)

§§ `Moves between Scotland and England and Wales (regs 23ZA to 23ZC)`

-- Reg 23ZA(1): Seren gets child disability payment, moves to Wales; the 13 week period of reg 36(1) of the 2021 Regulations applies and the day is in it.
#ASSERT `Is regulation 16(c) treated as not satisfied for me because I moved from Scotland` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- The day is outside the period.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is regulation 16(c) treated as not satisfied for me because I moved from Scotland` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 23ZA(2): the 2022 Regulations (adult disability payment).
#ASSERT `Is regulation 16(c) treated as not satisfied for me because I moved from Scotland` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Neither regulation applies.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is regulation 16(c) treated as not satisfied for me because I moved from Scotland` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 23ZB(2), (4): Hamish becomes permanently resident in Scotland on 1 December 2025, entitled the day before; the run-on period is the 13 weeks beginning 1 December 2025 and ends 1 March 2026. 1 December 2025 is the first day.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as present in England and Wales on this day after I move to Scotland` (YMD 2025 12 1) TRUE (YMD 2025 12 1)
-- Last day of the run-on period (1 December + 90 days = 1 March 2026).
#ASSERT `Am I treated as present in England and Wales on this day after I move to Scotland` (YMD 2025 12 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- The day after.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as present in England and Wales on this day after I move to Scotland` (YMD 2025 12 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 2))
-- The day before the move.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as present in England and Wales on this day after I move to Scotland` (YMD 2025 12 1) TRUE (YMD 2025 11 30))
-- Not entitled to a component the day before.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as present in England and Wales on this day after I move to Scotland` (YMD 2025 12 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 12 15))
-- Reg 23ZB(1): a move on 6 November 2025 itself is within "on or after 6th November 2025".
#ASSERT `Am I treated as present in England and Wales on this day after I move to Scotland` (YMD 2025 11 6) TRUE (YMD 2025 11 6)
-- A move on 5 November 2025 is not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as present in England and Wales on this day after I move to Scotland` (YMD 2025 11 5) TRUE (YMD 2025 11 5))
-- Reg 23ZB(3): his award is for a fixed term that expires on 20 December 2025, before the end of the run-on period: extended to 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `On what day does my fixed term award end after the extension` (YMD 2025 12 1) TRUE (YMD 2025 12 20) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- A fixed term due to expire on the last day of the run-on period is not due to expire before the end of it (fork F-31): unchanged.
#ASSERT `On what day does my fixed term award end after the extension` (YMD 2025 12 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- Expiring after the run-on period: unchanged.
#ASSERT `On what day does my fixed term award end after the extension` (YMD 2025 12 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 2) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 2)
-- No fixed term award: the day he gives is returned unchanged.
#ASSERT `On what day does my fixed term award end after the extension` (YMD 2025 12 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 12 20) EQUALS (YMD 2025 12 20)
-- Before 6 November 2025 reg 23ZB does not apply: unchanged.
#ASSERT `On what day does my fixed term award end after the extension` (YMD 2025 10 1) TRUE (YMD 2025 10 20) EQUALS (YMD 2025 10 20)
-- Reg 23ZC(3): Isla's claim has not been decided, withdrawn or otherwise ended: ongoing.
#ASSERT `Is my claim still ongoing on the date I become permanently resident in Scotland` FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Decided.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my claim still ongoing on the date I become permanently resident in Scotland` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Withdrawn.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my claim still ongoing on the date I become permanently resident in Scotland` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Otherwise ceased to be under consideration.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my claim still ongoing on the date I become permanently resident in Scotland` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Reg 23ZC(2)(c): present in England and Wales on 1 December 2025.
#ASSERT `Am I present or treated as present on this day for the purposes of regulation 23ZC` (YMD 2025 12 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Treated as present by another provision.
#ASSERT `Am I present or treated as present on this day for the purposes of regulation 23ZC` (YMD 2025 12 1) FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Present only in Great Britain (Scotland) on a day on or after 6 November 2025: not enough.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I present or treated as present on this day for the purposes of regulation 23ZC` (YMD 2025 12 1) FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Reg 23ZC(4): on a day before 6 November 2025 (5 November), treated as present in Great Britain is enough.
#ASSERT `Am I present or treated as present on this day for the purposes of regulation 23ZC` (YMD 2025 11 5) FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Boundary: 6 November 2025 itself is not "before 6th November 2025".
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I present or treated as present on this day for the purposes of regulation 23ZC` (YMD 2025 11 6) FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Reg 23ZC(1), (5): ongoing, resident in Scotland from 1 December 2025, present on the claim day and the day before: the Secretary of State must decide.
#ASSERT `Must the Secretary of State decide my claim under section 8 of the 1998 Act after my move to Scotland` TRUE (YMD 2025 12 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- She withdraws the claim under reg 31: no requirement.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Secretary of State decide my claim under section 8 of the 1998 Act after my move to Scotland` TRUE (YMD 2025 12 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Her claim was no longer ongoing.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Secretary of State decide my claim under section 8 of the 1998 Act after my move to Scotland` FALSE (YMD 2025 12 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Reg 23ZC(2)(b): she became resident in Scotland on 5 November 2025.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Secretary of State decide my claim under section 8 of the 1998 Act after my move to Scotland` TRUE (YMD 2025 11 5) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- She was not present on the day before.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Secretary of State decide my claim under section 8 of the 1998 Act after my move to Scotland` TRUE (YMD 2025 12 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 23ZC(7)(a): the Secretary of State decides she is entitled: treated as present in the run-on period (to 1 March 2026).
#ASSERT `Am I treated as present in England and Wales on this day after my move because my ongoing claim is decided` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 12 1) (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- After the run-on period.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as present in England and Wales on this day after my move because my ongoing claim is decided` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 12 1) (YMD 2026 3 2))
-- Not entitled.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as present in England and Wales on this day after my move because my ongoing claim is decided` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 12 1) (YMD 2025 12 15))
-- Reg 23ZC(5) did not require a decision.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as present in England and Wales on this day after my move because my ongoing claim is decided` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2025 12 1) (YMD 2025 12 15))
-- Reg 23ZC(7)(b): a fixed term award expiring on 20 December 2025 is extended to 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `On what day does my fixed term award end after the extension on a decision of my ongoing claim` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 12 1) TRUE (YMD 2025 12 20) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- Not entitled on the decision: unchanged.
#ASSERT `On what day does my fixed term award end after the extension on a decision of my ongoing claim` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 12 1) TRUE (YMD 2025 12 20) EQUALS (YMD 2025 12 20)

