§ `The weekly rate (Part 5) and reaching the relevant age (Part 6)`

§§ `What I am paid a week (reg 24)`

-- Reg 24(1)(a): the standard rate of the daily living component, 76.70 pounds a week.
#ASSERT `What is the weekly rate of this component at this rate` `the daily living component` `the standard rate of the component` EQUALS JUST 76.70
-- Reg 24(1)(b): the enhanced rate, 114.60.
#ASSERT `What is the weekly rate of this component at this rate` `the daily living component` `the enhanced rate of the component` EQUALS JUST 114.60
-- Reg 24(2)(a): the mobility component, standard rate, 30.30.
#ASSERT `What is the weekly rate of this component at this rate` `the mobility component` `the standard rate of the component` EQUALS JUST 30.30
-- Reg 24(2)(b): enhanced, 80.00.
#ASSERT `What is the weekly rate of this component at this rate` `the mobility component` `the enhanced rate of the component` EQUALS JUST 80.00
-- Not covered: no rate of a component, the regulation prescribes no amount.
#ASSERT `What is the weekly rate of this component at this rate` `the daily living component` `no rate of the component` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What is the weekly rate of this component at this rate` `the mobility component` `no rate of the component` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Reaching the relevant age (regs 25 to 27)`

-- Reg 25(a): Walter has reached the relevant age and was entitled to a component the day before.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 25 save my personal independence payment from section 83(1)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Reg 25(b): not entitled before, but he claimed before reaching the age, the claim was undetermined at that age, and an award would be made but for section 83(1).
#ASSERT `Does regulation 25 save my personal independence payment from section 83(1)` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- No award would be made but for section 83(1).
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 25 save my personal independence payment from section 83(1)` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- The claim was determined before he reached that age.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 25 save my personal independence payment from section 83(1)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- He made no claim before reaching the age.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 25 save my personal independence payment from section 83(1)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- He has not reached the relevant age: section 83(1) is not in play and regulation 25 does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 25 save my personal independence payment from section 83(1)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 26(1), (2)(a): Yasmin has reached the relevant age and makes a new claim in the circumstances of regulation 15.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 26 save my new claim after an interval from section 83(1)` TRUE TRUE
-- Her claim is not in the circumstances of regulation 15.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 26 save my new claim after an interval from section 83(1)` TRUE FALSE)
-- She has not reached the relevant age.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 26 save my new claim after an interval from section 83(1)` FALSE TRUE)
-- Reg 26(2)(c)(i): severely limited mobility, previously the enhanced rate: the enhanced rate.
#ASSERT `What rate of the mobility component can I get on my new claim after the relevant age` TRUE TRUE `severely limited ability` `the enhanced rate of the component` EQUALS JUST `the enhanced rate of the component`
-- Reg 26(2)(c)(ii): severely limited, previously the standard rate: the standard rate.
#ASSERT `What rate of the mobility component can I get on my new claim after the relevant age` TRUE TRUE `severely limited ability` `the standard rate of the component` EQUALS JUST `the standard rate of the component`
-- Reg 26(2)(c): severely limited but no mobility rate before (fork F-35): no rate.
#ASSERT `What rate of the mobility component can I get on my new claim after the relevant age` TRUE TRUE `severely limited ability` `no rate of the component` EQUALS JUST `no rate of the component`
-- Reg 26(2)(d): limited ability, previously the enhanced rate: the standard rate (entitled to the component at either rate).
#ASSERT `What rate of the mobility component can I get on my new claim after the relevant age` TRUE TRUE `limited ability` `the enhanced rate of the component` EQUALS JUST `the standard rate of the component`
-- Reg 26(2)(d): limited ability, previously the standard rate.
#ASSERT `What rate of the mobility component can I get on my new claim after the relevant age` TRUE TRUE `limited ability` `the standard rate of the component` EQUALS JUST `the standard rate of the component`
-- Reg 26(2)(d): limited ability, no mobility component before: no rate.
#ASSERT `What rate of the mobility component can I get on my new claim after the relevant age` TRUE TRUE `limited ability` `no rate of the component` EQUALS JUST `no rate of the component`
-- Neither level: no rate.
#ASSERT `What rate of the mobility component can I get on my new claim after the relevant age` TRUE TRUE `neither limited ability nor severely limited ability` `the enhanced rate of the component` EQUALS JUST `no rate of the component`
-- Not covered: she has not reached the relevant age, so regulation 26(2)(c) and (d) do not reach her.
#ASSERT `What rate of the mobility component can I get on my new claim after the relevant age` FALSE TRUE `severely limited ability` `the enhanced rate of the component` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Reg 26A(1), (2)(a): the same after Scottish adult disability living allowance.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 26A save my new claim after Scottish adult disability living allowance from section 83(1)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 26A save my new claim after Scottish adult disability living allowance from section 83(1)` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 26A save my new claim after Scottish adult disability living allowance from section 83(1)` FALSE TRUE)
-- Reg 27(1): Zara, past the relevant age, has an award saved by regulation 25 and it falls to be revised.
#ASSERT `Does section 83(1) not apply when my saved award is revised or superseded` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does section 83(1) not apply when my saved award is revised or superseded` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does section 83(1) not apply when my saved award is revised or superseded` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does section 83(1) not apply when my saved award is revised or superseded` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Reg 27(2)(a): Zara reached the relevant age on 1 January 2025; her mobility award is superseded under reg 23 for a change of circumstances on 1 August 2025, after that date: the restrictions of reg 27(3) apply.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions of regulation 27(3) apply when my mobility component award is superseded, Secretary of State version` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 8 1) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- The change was on 1 December 2024, before she reached the age.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the restrictions of regulation 27(3) apply when my mobility component award is superseded, Secretary of State version` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2024 12 1) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1))
-- The change was on the day she reached the age (1 January 2025): not "after".
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the restrictions of regulation 27(3) apply when my mobility component award is superseded, Secretary of State version` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1))
-- The day after.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions of regulation 27(3) apply when my mobility component award is superseded, Secretary of State version` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 1 2) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- Reg 27(2)(b)(i): superseded under reg 26(1)(a) on her application made on 1 March 2025, after the relevant age.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions of regulation 27(3) apply when my mobility component award is superseded, Secretary of State version` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- Her application was made on 1 November 2024, before.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the restrictions of regulation 27(3) apply when my mobility component award is superseded, Secretary of State version` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) TRUE TRUE (YMD 2024 11 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1))
-- Reg 27(2)(b)(ii): the Secretary of State initiated the proceedings on 1 April 2025, after.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions of regulation 27(3) apply when my mobility component award is superseded, Secretary of State version` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2025 4 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- ... and on 1 December 2024, before.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the restrictions of regulation 27(3) apply when my mobility component award is superseded, Secretary of State version` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2024 12 1) (YMD 2025 1 1))
-- Her original award does not include the mobility component.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the restrictions of regulation 27(3) apply when my mobility component award is superseded, Secretary of State version` FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 8 1) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1))
-- The second version of reg 27(2) (fork F-32): initiated by the Scottish Ministers on 1 April 2025, after.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions of regulation 27(3) apply when my mobility component award is superseded, Scottish Ministers version` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2025 4 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- ... before.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the restrictions of regulation 27(3) apply when my mobility component award is superseded, Scottish Ministers version` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2024 12 1) (YMD 2025 1 1))
-- A change of circumstances after the age, under the Scottish Ministers version.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions of regulation 27(3) apply when my mobility component award is superseded, Scottish Ministers version` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 8 1) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- Reg 27(3)(a): the original award was for the standard rate; the Secretary of State may award the standard rate if entitlement results from the same condition.
#ASSERT `May the Secretary of State award me this rate of the mobility component in place of my original award` `the standard rate of the component` `the standard rate of the component` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- ... not if from a different condition.
#ASSERT `May the Secretary of State award me this rate of the mobility component in place of my original award` `the standard rate of the component` `the standard rate of the component` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Reg 27(3)(a)(i): never the enhanced rate where the original was standard.
#ASSERT `May the Secretary of State award me this rate of the mobility component in place of my original award` `the standard rate of the component` `the enhanced rate of the component` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Reg 27(3)(b): original enhanced, the enhanced rate only where entitlement results from the same condition.
#ASSERT `May the Secretary of State award me this rate of the mobility component in place of my original award` `the enhanced rate of the component` `the enhanced rate of the component` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the Secretary of State award me this rate of the mobility component in place of my original award` `the enhanced rate of the component` `the enhanced rate of the component` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered (fork F-33): the original was enhanced and the proposed rate is standard; reg 27(3)(b) is silent.
#ASSERT `May the Secretary of State award me this rate of the mobility component in place of my original award` `the enhanced rate of the component` `the standard rate of the component` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not covered: the original award had no mobility rate.
#ASSERT `May the Secretary of State award me this rate of the mobility component in place of my original award` `no rate of the component` `the standard rate of the component` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Reg 27(4): Zara's original award has no mobility component but she had one that ceased on 15 June 2024, exactly 1 year before the supersession takes effect (15 June 2025).
#ASSERT `Does my previous mobility component award count as my original award` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2024 6 15) (YMD 2025 6 15)
-- It ceased on 14 June 2024: more than 1 year.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my previous mobility component award count as my original award` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2024 6 14) (YMD 2025 6 15))
-- Her original award includes the mobility component: nothing to treat.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my previous mobility component award count as my original award` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2024 6 15) (YMD 2025 6 15))
-- She never had a mobility award.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my previous mobility component award count as my original award` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2024 6 15) (YMD 2025 6 15))

§ `Payment while in a care home, a hospital or custody (Part 7)`

§§ `Periods of residence (reg 32)`

-- Reg 32(2)(a): Pauline enters a care home on 10 March 2025; the period begins the next day.
#ASSERT `On what day does my period of residence begin` (YMD 2025 3 10) EQUALS (YMD 2025 3 11)
-- Reg 32(2)(b): she leaves on 20 April 2025; the period ends the day before.
#ASSERT `On what day does my period of residence end` (YMD 2025 4 20) FALSE EQUALS (YMD 2025 4 19)
-- Reg 32(3): she moves from the care home straight into hospital on 20 April 2025; the earlier period ends on the day she leaves.
#ASSERT `On what day does my period of residence end` (YMD 2025 4 20) TRUE EQUALS (YMD 2025 4 20)
-- Reg 32(1): in a care home (s85(2)), in a hospital (s86(2)), or in custody; or none.
#ASSERT `Am I in a period of residence` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I in a period of residence` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I in a period of residence` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I in a period of residence` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 32(4): one period entered on 10 March 2025 (it begins 11 March) and left on 20 April 2025 (it ends 19 April). On 1 April: 11 March to 1 April is 22 days.
#ASSERT `How many days of residence have I accumulated in my continuous period up to this day` (YMD 2025 4 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 3 10) (YMD 2025 4 20) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE EQUALS JUST 22
-- On 19 April, the last day: 11 March to 19 April is 40 days.
#ASSERT `How many days of residence have I accumulated in my continuous period up to this day` (YMD 2025 4 19) FALSE (YMD 2025 3 10) (YMD 2025 4 20) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE EQUALS JUST 40
-- Not covered: on 20 April, the day she leaves, she is in no period of residence.
#ASSERT `How many days of residence have I accumulated in my continuous period up to this day` (YMD 2025 4 20) FALSE (YMD 2025 3 10) (YMD 2025 4 20) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not covered: nor on 10 March, the day she enters.
#ASSERT `How many days of residence have I accumulated in my continuous period up to this day` (YMD 2025 3 10) FALSE (YMD 2025 3 10) (YMD 2025 4 20) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Reg 32(4)(a): Raj's first period ran 2 January to 30 January 2025 (29 days); his second began 28 February 2025: the interval is 28 days (31 January to 27 February), so the periods join; on 10 March the continuous period is 29 + 11 = 40 days.
#ASSERT `How many days of residence have I accumulated in my continuous period up to this day` (YMD 2025 3 10) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 31) FALSE TRUE (YMD 2025 2 27) (YMD 2025 5 1) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE EQUALS JUST 40
-- If the second period began 1 March 2025 the interval is 29 days: the periods do not join, and on 10 March only the second counts: 10 days.
#ASSERT `How many days of residence have I accumulated in my continuous period up to this day` (YMD 2025 3 10) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 31) FALSE TRUE (YMD 2025 2 28) (YMD 2025 5 1) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE EQUALS JUST 10
-- Reg 32(5): both periods are periods to which section 87 applies (prison), so the limit is one year; the second period began 2 December 2025 and on 10 December the continuous period is 29 + 9 = 38 days.
#ASSERT `How many days of residence have I accumulated in my continuous period up to this day` (YMD 2025 12 10) TRUE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 31) FALSE TRUE (YMD 2025 12 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE EQUALS JUST 38
-- The same facts when they are not section 87 periods: the gap is over 28 days, so only 9.
#ASSERT `How many days of residence have I accumulated in my continuous period up to this day` (YMD 2025 12 10) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 31) FALSE TRUE (YMD 2025 12 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE EQUALS JUST 9
-- Three periods in a chain: 2 to 30 January (29 days), 28 February to 31 March (32 days), and from 29 April; on 10 May the third has run 12 days: 29 + 32 + 12 = 73.
#ASSERT `How many days of residence have I accumulated in my continuous period up to this day` (YMD 2025 5 10) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 31) FALSE TRUE (YMD 2025 2 27) (YMD 2025 4 1) FALSE TRUE (YMD 2025 4 28) (YMD 2025 6 30) FALSE EQUALS JUST 73

§§ `Care homes (regs 28, 30)`

-- Reg 28(2)(a): Ahmed's care home services are provided and their costs borne out of public funds under Part 3 of the National Assistance Act 1948.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the care home condition of section 85(2) of the Act` TRUE TRUE `Part 3 of the National Assistance Act 1948`
-- Reg 28(2)(eea): Part 1 of the Care Act 2014.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the care home condition of section 85(2) of the Act` TRUE TRUE `Part 1 of the Care Act 2014`
-- Reg 28(2)(f): any other enactment relating to persons under a disability.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the care home condition of section 85(2) of the Act` TRUE TRUE `any other enactment relating to persons under a disability or to young persons or to education or training`
-- Reg 28(2)(f)(i): section 485 of the Education Act 1996 is excepted.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I meet the care home condition of section 85(2) of the Act` TRUE TRUE `section 485 of the Education Act 1996`)
-- Reg 28(2)(f)(ii): section 14 of the Education Act 2002.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I meet the care home condition of section 85(2) of the Act` TRUE TRUE `section 14 of the Education Act 2002`)
-- Reg 28(2)(f)(vii): section 39 or 40 of the Higher Education and Research Act 2017.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I meet the care home condition of section 85(2) of the Act` TRUE TRUE `section 39 or section 40 of the Higher Education and Research Act 2017`)
-- An enactment of some other kind is not specified.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I meet the care home condition of section 85(2) of the Act` TRUE TRUE `an enactment of some other kind`)
-- The costs are borne by Ahmed himself: not borne out of public or local funds.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I meet the care home condition of section 85(2) of the Act` TRUE FALSE `Part 3 of the National Assistance Act 1948`)
-- No qualifying services in a care home.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I meet the care home condition of section 85(2) of the Act` FALSE TRUE `Part 3 of the National Assistance Act 1948`)
-- Reg 28(3)(a)(ii), (4): Ben is 16, section 17(10)(c) of the Children Act 1989 applies (disability) and the local authority places him in a private dwelling with a family.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 28(1) not apply to me because of my age and placement` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Reg 28(3)(a)(i): section 17(10)(b), the health of a child likely to be impaired.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 28(1) not apply to me because of my age and placement` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Reg 28(4): the same, but placed in a children's home: the exception applies only while placed in a private dwelling.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 28(1) not apply to me because of my age and placement` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 28(3)(aa): section 37 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014 applies, placed with a relative.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 28(1) not apply to me because of my age and placement` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- At 18 the child provisions no longer help.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 28(1) not apply to me because of my age and placement` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 28(3)(b): accommodated outside the United Kingdom at a local authority's cost under section 320 of the Education Act 1996.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 28(1) not apply to me because of my age and placement` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Accommodated outside the United Kingdom but the costs are not borne by a local authority.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 28(1) not apply to me because of my age and placement` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Reg 30(1): Ahmed's 28th day of residence: payment goes on.
#ASSERT `Does my payment go on because this day is among the first 28 days` TRUE 28 FALSE
-- Day 29: it does not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my payment go on because this day is among the first 28 days` TRUE 29 FALSE)
-- Day 1.
#ASSERT `Does my payment go on because this day is among the first 28 days` TRUE 1 FALSE
-- Reg 30(2): he was already in the care home when his entitlement commenced, and this day is in the run of days beginning with that day: paragraph (1) does not apply to him, so payment does not go on.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my payment go on because this day is among the first 28 days` TRUE 10 TRUE)
-- Not in a period of residence on the day: nothing to count.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my payment go on because this day is among the first 28 days` FALSE 0 FALSE)
-- Reg 30(4): the Marie Curie style hospice: primary function palliative care, none of the exclusions.
#ASSERT `Is the place where I live a hospice` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A health service hospital in England is excluded.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the place where I live a hospice` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- A Welsh NHS hospital.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the place where I live a hospice` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- A health service hospital in Scotland.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the place where I live a hospice` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- A Defence Council hospital.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the place where I live a hospice` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- An institution similar to those.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the place where I live a hospice` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- A nursing home with another primary function.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the place where I live a hospice` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 30(3): Greta is in a hospice, terminally ill, and the Secretary of State was told on her claim.
#ASSERT `Do regulations 28 and 29 not apply to me because I am terminally ill in a hospice` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Told in writing in connection with the award.
#ASSERT `Do regulations 28 and 29 not apply to me because I am terminally ill in a hospice` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Told on an application for revision.
#ASSERT `Do regulations 28 and 29 not apply to me because I am terminally ill in a hospice` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- The Secretary of State has not been told.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do regulations 28 and 29 not apply to me because I am terminally ill in a hospice` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Not terminally ill.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do regulations 28 and 29 not apply to me because I am terminally ill in a hospice` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Not in a hospice.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do regulations 28 and 29 not apply to me because I am terminally ill in a hospice` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 30(5): Ahmed pays the whole cost out of his own resources.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 28(1) not apply to me because the whole cost is met from private means` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Part his own resources, part a charity.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 28(1) not apply to me because the whole cost is met from private means` FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- His daughter pays on his behalf.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 28(1) not apply to me because the whole cost is met from private means` FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- The local authority pays.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 28(1) not apply to me because the whole cost is met from private means` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 28(1): Ahmed meets the care home condition and no exception applies: no amount attributable to the daily living component is payable.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is an amount attributable to my daily living component payable for this day while I am in a care home` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- He does not meet the condition: payable.
#ASSERT `Is an amount attributable to my daily living component payable for this day while I am in a care home` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Reg 28(3) applies: payable.
#ASSERT `Is an amount attributable to my daily living component payable for this day while I am in a care home` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Within the first 28 days: payable.
#ASSERT `Is an amount attributable to my daily living component payable for this day while I am in a care home` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Terminally ill in a hospice (reg 30(3)): payable.
#ASSERT `Is an amount attributable to my daily living component payable for this day while I am in a care home` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Private means (reg 30(5)): payable.
#ASSERT `Is an amount attributable to my daily living component payable for this day while I am in a care home` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

§§ `Hospital in-patients (regs 29, 30)`

-- Reg 29(2)(a)(i): Chloe is an in-patient at an NHS hospital in England.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the hospital in-patient condition of section 86(2) of the Act` TRUE `a hospital or similar institution under the National Health Service Act 2006`
-- Reg 29(2)(a)(ii): Wales.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the hospital in-patient condition of section 86(2) of the Act` TRUE `a hospital or similar institution under the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006`
-- Reg 29(2)(a)(iii): Scotland.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the hospital in-patient condition of section 86(2) of the Act` TRUE `a hospital or similar institution under the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978`
-- Reg 29(2)(b): a hospital maintained by the Defence Council.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the hospital in-patient condition of section 86(2) of the Act` TRUE `a hospital or similar institution maintained or administered by the Defence Council`
-- A private hospital paid for by her: not one of the institutions.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I meet the hospital in-patient condition of section 86(2) of the Act` TRUE `some other institution`)
-- She is an out-patient.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I meet the hospital in-patient condition of section 86(2) of the Act` FALSE `a hospital or similar institution under the National Health Service Act 2006`)
-- Reg 29(3): Chloe was born 15 June 2008 and entered hospital on 14 June 2026, the day before her 18th birthday: under 18 on the day of entry.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 29 not apply to me because I was under 18 when I entered hospital` (YMD 2008 6 15) (YMD 2026 6 14)
-- She entered on her 18th birthday, 15 June 2026: not under 18.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 29 not apply to me because I was under 18 when I entered hospital` (YMD 2008 6 15) (YMD 2026 6 15))
-- Reg 29(1): meets the condition, nothing else: no amount attributable to either component is payable.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is an amount attributable to my components payable for this day while I am in hospital` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Not an in-patient: payable.
#ASSERT `Is an amount attributable to my components payable for this day while I am in hospital` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Under 18 on entry: payable.
#ASSERT `Is an amount attributable to my components payable for this day while I am in hospital` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- First 28 days: payable.
#ASSERT `Is an amount attributable to my components payable for this day while I am in hospital` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Hospice and terminally ill: payable.
#ASSERT `Is an amount attributable to my components payable for this day while I am in hospital` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE

§§ `Prisoners and detainees (reg 31)`

-- Reg 31(1): Kwame is in prison, day 28 of his period: payment goes on.
#ASSERT `Does my payment go on in custody because this day is among the first 28 days` TRUE 28 FALSE
-- Day 29.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my payment go on in custody because this day is among the first 28 days` TRUE 29 FALSE)
-- Reg 31(2): he was in custody when his entitlement commenced: paragraph (1) does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my payment go on in custody because this day is among the first 28 days` TRUE 10 TRUE)
-- Not in a period of residence.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my payment go on in custody because this day is among the first 28 days` FALSE 0 FALSE)
-- Reg 31(5)(a): a secure hospital: persons suffering from mental disorder are received there, not a prison or in one.
#ASSERT `Is the place where I am detained a hospital or similar institution` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- A prison.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the place where I am detained a hospital or similar institution` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- A hospital wing at a prison ("at or in" such a place).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the place where I am detained a hospital or similar institution` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- No mentally disordered persons are received there.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the place where I am detained a hospital or similar institution` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 31(5)(b): found insane, so he cannot be tried.
#ASSERT `Are the criminal proceedings against me deemed concluded` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Are the criminal proceedings against me deemed concluded` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Are the criminal proceedings against me deemed concluded` FALSE TRUE)
-- Reg 31(4)(a): Kwame is detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983 on 1 June 2025, his certified release date.
#ASSERT `Do I satisfy one of the conditions of regulation 31(4)` TRUE (YMD 2025 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2025 6 1) FALSE FALSE
-- The day after his certified release date, 2 June 2025... shown by a certified date of 31 May: past it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I satisfy one of the conditions of regulation 31(4)` TRUE (YMD 2025 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2025 5 31) FALSE FALSE)
-- No release date certified: reg 31(4)(a)(ii) not satisfied.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I satisfy one of the conditions of regulation 31(4)` TRUE (YMD 2025 6 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 6 1) FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 31(4)(b)(i): a hospital direction under section 59A of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995.
#ASSERT `Do I satisfy one of the conditions of regulation 31(4)` FALSE (YMD 2025 6 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 6 1) TRUE FALSE
-- Reg 31(4)(b)(ii): transfer under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003.
#ASSERT `Do I satisfy one of the conditions of regulation 31(4)` FALSE (YMD 2025 6 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 6 1) FALSE TRUE
-- None.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I satisfy one of the conditions of regulation 31(4)` FALSE (YMD 2025 6 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 6 1) FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 31(3): detained in a hospital in Great Britain after the proceedings concluded and satisfying neither condition of paragraph (4): section 87 does not apply.
#ASSERT `Does section 87 not apply to me because my criminal proceedings concluded and I am detained in hospital` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- If he satisfies a condition of paragraph (4), it does not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does section 87 not apply to me because my criminal proceedings concluded and I am detained in hospital` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- The proceedings have not concluded.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does section 87 not apply to me because my criminal proceedings concluded and I am detained in hospital` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Not detained in such a hospital.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does section 87 not apply to me because my criminal proceedings concluded and I am detained in hospital` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Reg 31(6): Kwame is imprisoned in France, and in similar circumstances in Great Britain he would have been excepted.
#ASSERT `Does section 87 not apply to me because I am in custody outside Great Britain` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does section 87 not apply to me because I am in custody outside Great Britain` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does section 87 not apply to me because I am in custody outside Great Britain` FALSE TRUE)
-- Reg 31: section 87 applies and no exception applies: no amount is payable.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is an amount of personal independence payment payable for this day while I am in custody` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Section 87 does not apply to him on the day: payable.
#ASSERT `Is an amount of personal independence payment payable for this day while I am in custody` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- First 28 days: payable.
#ASSERT `Is an amount of personal independence payment payable for this day while I am in custody` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Reg 31(3): payable.
#ASSERT `Is an amount of personal independence payment payable for this day while I am in custody` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Reg 31(6): payable.
#ASSERT `Is an amount of personal independence payment payable for this day while I am in custody` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
